KASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIBATA, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKADA TATSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIBANUMA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIBATA NORIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKADA, TATSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIBANUMA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIBATA, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Before at least one specific material selected from among 1,1,1,3,3-pentachloropropane, 1,1,3,3,-tetrachloropropene and 1,3,3,3-tetrachloropropene is fluorinated by reacting with HF, moisture is sufficiently eliminated from the material(s). When useful 1,1,1,3,3-pentafluoropropane and/or 1-chloro-3,3,3-trifluoropropene are produced by fluorinating specific material(s) with HF in the presence of a catalyst, the inactivation of the catalyst and the accumulation of high-boiling matters are prevented to thereby continuously produce the above useful target product efficiently.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Le procédé de l'invention consiste à prendre au moins un matériau spécifique tel que 1,1,1,3,3-pentachloropropane, 1,1,3,3,-tétrachloropropène et 1,3,3,3-tétrachloropropène, à le déshydrater, puis à le fluorer par réaction avec l'acide fluorhydrique. Une fois qu'on a obtenu le 1,1,1,3,3-pentafluoropropane et/ou le 1-chloro-3,3,3-trifluoropropène par fluoration des matériaux spécifiques considérés au moyen d'acide fluorhydrique en présence d'un catalyseur, l'inactivation du catalyseur et l'accumulation de matières à point d'ébullition élevé devient impossible ce qui permet une bonne production en continu des produits cibles utiles de l'invention.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>